# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# The app routes with BrowserRouter, so /patients and /settings are paths the
# browser really asks the server for — on a refresh, on a bookmark, and on
# every link somebody pastes into WhatsApp. Pages looks for a file at that
# path, finds none, and serves its 404.
#
# 200, not 302: the URL in the address bar has to survive, because the router
# reads it to decide what to render. A redirect would send every deep link to
# the dashboard.
#
# /api/* is deliberately absent. The API is a separate origin reached over the
# tunnel, and a rule here would silently swallow a mis-built VITE_API_URL that
# should fail loudly instead.
/*    /index.html   200
